  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Fan Tan (Sevens). Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Fan Tan, also widely known as 'Sevens', 'Domino', or 'Parliament', is a classic layout-based card game where the objective is to be the first to get rid of all your cards. Players build upon a central layout of cards, starting with the Sevens and expanding outward to the Ace and Two in each suit. It is a game of both luck and light strategy, as players can choose to hold back key 'blocking' cards to prevent opponents from playing.",
    objective: 'Play and collect Alice-themed cards according to the published nineteenth-century rules.',
    gameplay: 'The deck is divided into starred picture cards, plain picture cards, and numbered cards. Because the source identifies the custom deck structure, this record keeps it separate from ordinary matching games.',
    keyRules: [
      'Published by Selchow and Righter in 1882.',
      'Uses three classes of cards: starred pictures, plain pictures, and numbered cards.',
      'Based on Alice in Wonderland and old enough to treat as a historical game record.',
    ],
